\description{
\code{BlackScholes} prices an option from its underlying's price and \code{Black76} from a forward price, such as a future's. Each holds one option's inputs and reports its fair price and its five greeks as read-only fields, and each has an \code{implied_volatility()} function on its class generator that finds the volatility at which the model reproduces a premium seen in the market. \code{Option} uses Black-76 when the option's underlying is a future and Black-Scholes otherwise, and the models can be used on their own with any figures.

The models assume no dividends and a European option, one exercised only at expiry. Theta is given per calendar day, and vega and rho per percentage point, which is how brokers' option chains show them.

A subclass takes the price it models from, the strike, the time to expiry, the rate, the volatility and the side, in that order, keeps the volatility in a public \code{volatility} field, and reports \code{price} and the greeks as active bindings. This class needs nothing else from it, so the search works for any model that follows that shape.
